    "lineStart": 0,
    "memoText": " \n                          VETO MESSAGE - No. 30\n \nTO THE SENATE:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nSenate Bill Number 5426, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend the real property law, in relation to increasing\n      the period of supervision required for certain real estate license\n      applications\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  This bill would increase the  amount  of  time  licensed  real  estate\nsalespersons  seeking  to  become  licensed  real estate brokers must be\nsupervised by a broker from two years to five consecutive years.\n \n  I am committed to protecting homeowners and homebuyers  in  New  York,\nwhich is why last year I enacted landmark legislation criminalizing deed\ntheft scams, and why I recently proposed and signed legislation to safe-\nguard against appraisal discrimination.\n \n  However, this bill would unduly increase experiential requirements for\nbecoming  a  real  estate broker to levels that substantially exceed the\nstandards in even those states referenced in the  Sponsor's  Memo.  This\nwould  erect  burdensome  barriers that could hinder efforts to ensure a\nhealthy and diverse broker marketplace.\n \n  Therefore, I am constrained to veto this bill.\n \n  The bill is disapproved.                       (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
    "vetoNumber": 30,
    "vetoType": "STANDARD",
